const experience=b('Experience','经验'),hypothesis=b('Metaphysical hypothesis','形而上假设'),inference=b('Conditional inference','条件性推论'),revision=b('Model revision','模型修正'),distinction=b('Conceptual distinction','概念区分'),open=b('Open question','开放问题');
export const acts=[
  {id:'experience',scene:0,title:b('Before a theory,<br>a feeling.','理论之前，<br>是一次体验。'),deck:b('It began with a landscape—and with the body that made the landscape available to me.','起点是一片风景，以及让我得以体验它的身体。'),symbol:'World → body → experience',caption:b('The scenery stays. The world available to attention changes.','风景没有消失，能够进入注意力的世界却改变了。'),kind:experience,notes:[
    {n:1,type:experience,title:b('Why does discomfort make the world smaller?','身体一不舒服，整个世界为什么都会变窄？'),p:[
      b('I was looking at mountains, trees, sky, and a road passing before me. My body felt comfortable; my mind was quiet. For a moment, the scene seemed almost like a game. A game can render mountains, weather, light, and cities. But what makes reality so immediate is that the body participates in it.','一次在路上看风景，身体舒服，心里平静。山、树、天空和道路从眼前经过，突然觉得这一切有点像游戏。游戏可以模拟山川、天气、光影和城市，但现实真正强烈的地方，是身体会参与其中。'),
      b('The same beautiful view can become inaccessible when I am uncomfortable. Pain, fatigue, tension, or scattered attention pull experience back toward the body. Telling myself that discomfort is “part of the world” does not make it disappear. The external scene has not become smaller; the range of experience I can enter has.','同一片漂亮风景，在身体不舒服时可能完全无法欣赏。疼痛、疲惫、发紧、精神涣散，会把注意力拉回身体。告诉自己“不舒服也是世界的一部分”，并不会让它消失。外部世界没有缩小，是主体能够进入的体验空间缩小了。'),
      b('Another morning, I wanted to sleep longer, but my back felt tense and my thoughts kept running. There was a cat, traffic, and noise outside. Yet the obstacle was not only external: my internal state would not obey the command to rest. Even “be still” was difficult to carry out. Perhaps “I control my body” gives the “I” more authority than it actually has.','后来一次早起，想多睡一会儿，却后背发紧、思绪不停。猫在闹，窗外有车与声音，但关键不只是外界：身体内部状态本身不允许进入休眠。连“静下来”也不是一个随时可以执行的命令。我们说“我控制我的身体”，也许高估了“我”的权限。')],pull:b('The world did not shrink. My access to it did.','世界没有缩小。我进入世界的能力，缩小了。')}
  ]},
  {id:'rules',scene:1,title:b('The strange thing<br>is “cannot.”','真正奇怪的，<br>是“不能”。'),deck:b('A limit stops being ordinary once I ask why it exists at all.','当我开始追问限制为何存在，熟悉的规则也变得陌生。'),symbol:'Possible / impossible',caption:b('A boundary is a way of selecting what can happen.','边界裁剪了哪些事情可以发生。'),kind:hypothesis,notes:[
    {n:2,type:hypothesis,title:b('From the body to the existence of rules','从身体走向规则'),p:[
      b('“Why can’t I sleep?” became “Why can’t I make myself sleep?” I cannot simply will pain away, turn the sky red, read another person’s mind, move instantly, reverse time, or cancel aging. We call these limits biology, physics, and causality. Their familiarity can hide how peculiar a prohibition is: some possibilities are admitted; others are excluded.','“为什么我睡不着”，逐渐变成“为什么我不能让自己睡着”。我不能凭意念取消疼痛、把天空变红、直接知道别人的思想、瞬间移动、逆转时间或取消衰老。这些限制被叫作身体规律、自然规律、因果关系。熟悉让我们忘了：规则在裁剪可能性。'),
      b('I began with a proposed ontological starting point: if a level of existence has specific constraints, I will not yet regard it as ultimate. Why these constraints, rather than others? This is a chosen premise of the framework, not a theorem established by logic. A particular rule is treated as a sign that something has already been delimited.','于是我提出一个本体论起点：凡具有特定规则和限制的存在层，暂时不把它当作终极层。为什么偏偏是这些限制，而不是另一套？这不是由形式逻辑证明的定理，而是框架选择的前提：规则被视为“已经被限定”的痕迹。')]},
    {n:3,type:hypothesis,title:b('“No rules” need not mean chaos','“无规则”不一定意味着混乱'),p:[
      b('At first, “without rules” sounded like randomness. I revised the meaning: an ultimate level would have no higher external prohibition. If something can still declare “it cannot do that,” the declaration seems to introduce a constraint above it. I provisionally called this imagined ground “Everything is possible.”','“无规则”最初容易被理解为随机与混乱。后来我重新定义它：最根本层不存在更高的外在禁止。如果还能说“它不能这样”，这句话似乎又在它之上加了一条限制。我暂时把这个设想称为 Everything is possible。'),
      b('This does not require every possibility to occur chaotically at once. In the proposal, a highly stable, internally constrained world is itself among the possibilities. Saying that the unrestricted cannot contain rules would add another prohibition. Rules could therefore be contents of the imagined ground, rather than restrictions upon it. But permitting such a world is not yet an explanation of why it appears.','它不要求所有事情混乱地同时发生。一个内部高度稳定、受到严密约束的世界，也可以属于可能性。若规定“无规则不能包含规则”，又加入了禁止。因此，在这一设想里，规则可以是它的内容，而不是它的限制。但允许规则世界出现，仍不等于解释了它为何出现。')],pull:b('Rules may be the contents of a deeper possibility, rather than its limits.','规则可能是更深可能性的内容，而非它的限制。')}
  ]},
  {id:'outside',scene:2,title:b('Can an inside<br>describe an outside?','内部的语言，<br>能描述外部吗？'),deck:b('The insect in a game became a way to examine the reach of our own concepts.','游戏里的虫子，成为检验我们概念边界的比喻。'),symbol:'W ⊂ ? ',caption:b('Nested frames illustrate a hypothesis about levels, not physical dimensions.','嵌套边框表达层级假设，并非物理维度。'),kind:hypothesis,notes:[
    {n:4,type:hypothesis,title:b('The insect inside a game','游戏里的虫子'),p:[
      b('Imagine a conscious insect inside a game. It studies mountains, cities, animals, and weather. It discovers that movement takes time, information travels at a limited speed, and energy is constrained. Then it calculates the resources needed to simulate its world and concludes that no computer could possibly do it.','假设游戏里有一只有意识、能研究自然规律的虫子。它发现移动需要时间、信息传播有限、能量受到约束。于是它估算模拟整个世界所需的资源，并得出“不可能被模拟”的结论。'),
      b('From outside the game, however, distance, energy, time, and computation may not mean what they mean inside it. A vast distance might be a difference between coordinates. Ten thousand internal years need not correspond to the same external duration. The insect might not even possess the concepts needed to describe the outside. The thought experiment questions an inference across levels; it does not establish that our world is simulated.','但在游戏外，距离、能量、时间与计算未必对应内部的同一概念。巨大距离也许只是坐标差，一万年未必对应同一种外部时长。虫子甚至可能没有描述外部所需的概念。这个比喻质疑跨层推断，并不证明我们的世界是模拟的。'),
      b('Even a more powerful external computer would still be subject to some structure. That would move the question, not finish it. “Simulation” gradually became too narrow a word for what I was asking. The deeper question was why there are rules at all.','即使外面是一台更强的计算机，它仍然受到某种结构限制。问题只是被推远，并没有结束。因此“模拟”逐渐变得太窄，真正的问题转向：规则为什么存在？')]},
    {n:5,type:hypothesis,title:b('Could levels interact?','规则外能否渗透规则内？'),p:[
      b('If a higher level existed, would it necessarily be sealed off? The model can imagine a closed world, an informational opening, an authorization to act, or a higher-level presence entering in a limited form. Traditional ideas of gods, immortals, revelation, and unusual experience gain possible places in that structure. Their possible placement is not evidence that any particular story happened.','如果更高层存在，它与低层是否必然隔绝？模型可以设想完全封闭、信息渗透、能力授权，或高层以有限形式进入低层。神、仙、启示与异常体验，在结构上因此获得候选位置。但结构上的位置，不证明任何具体故事发生过。'),
      b('Dreams, meditation, a feeling of unity, and anomalous experiences can also have internal explanations. An explanatory gap does not establish an outside cause. If cross-level information exists, the difficult question is what stable, distinguishable trace could separate it from error, coincidence, or a mechanism we do not yet understand.','梦、冥想、一体感和异常体验，也可能有内部解释。解释的空白，不等于规则外的原因。如果跨层信息确实存在，必须追问：什么稳定、可区分的痕迹，能把它与误判、巧合或尚未知晓的内部机制区分开？')],formula:b('Structurally allowed ≠ empirically established','结构上允许 ≠ 现实中已经发生')}
  ]},
  {id:'histories',scene:3,title:b('The first<br>model breaks.','第一个模型，<br>遇到了矛盾。'),deck:b('If anything is possible, why does the world not change completely every second?','如果一切皆可能，为什么世界不每秒彻底改变？'),symbol:'W₁(t) · W₂(t) · W₃(t)',caption:b('Several complete histories share a past, then differ. The curves are conceptual, not probabilities.','几条完整历史共享前缀，随后不同。曲线是概念示意，不表示概率。'),kind:revision,notes:[
    {n:6,type:revision,title:b('Stability becomes the objection','稳定性成为反对意见'),p:[
      b('“Everything is possible” immediately created a problem. Why has gravity not disappeared, why do people not suddenly become cats, and why does the world not turn magical? My first attempt was probability: perhaps continuation is overwhelmingly likely and radical change is rare. But the probability distribution is another structure. Why that distribution? What selects its weights?','“一切皆可能”很快带来危机：重力为什么没有突然消失，人为什么没有突然变成猫，世界为什么没有变成魔法体系？我先想到概率：也许连续规则的概率极高，剧变极低。但概率分布本身又是一套结构。为什么是这个分布？权重由什么决定？'),
      b('I also corrected a separate mistake: infinitely many possibilities do not imply equal probabilities. An infinite collection can carry very uneven weights. That repairs a mathematical intuition without explaining why a particular weighting exists. Probability can describe a rule-governed layer; it does not automatically explain the ultimate ground.','我同时修正另一个直觉：无数种可能，不意味着每种结果等概率。无限集合可以承载极不均匀的权重。这修正了数学直觉，却没有解释权重从何而来。概率可以描述某一规则层的统计结构，却不能自动成为终极解释。'),
      b('The model changed. Instead of imagining one world drawing a fresh result each second, I began considering complete possible worlds, each with an entire internal history. Their actual coexistence remains a metaphysical hypothesis.','于是模型发生转向：不再想象一个世界每秒重新抽签，而开始考虑各自具有完整内部历史的可能世界。它们是否实际并存，仍是形而上的假设。')]},
    {n:7,type:hypothesis,title:b('All the tracks, already whole','所有赛道，作为完整结构'),p:[
      b('World A might follow ordinary rules throughout. World B might include an extraordinary event at age twenty. World C might change its rules later. In this model, A does not suddenly jump into B; A, B, and C are separate complete structures. Several race tracks can share their first hundred kilometers and diverge afterward. The driver cannot determine the whole track from the road already traveled.','世界 A 可以始终维持普通规律；世界 B 可以在二十岁发生一次超常事件；世界 C 可以在未来改变规则。它们不是 A 突然跳成 B，而是分别作为完整结构存在。很多赛道前一百公里可以相同，后来才分开。车内的人不能仅凭已走过的路，确定整条赛道。'),
      b('The image of complete videos takes the analogy further. Each has its own internal time order. Some histories contain stable memory, bodily continuity, causal relations, and a self-model. They may thereby contain observers. The order of explanation reverses: not a pre-existing “me” placed into a world, but a world whose internal processes give rise to a particular “me.”','完整视频的比喻更进一步：每一条内部都有自己的时间顺序。有些历史具有稳定记忆、身体连续、因果关系与自我模型，于是其中可能出现观察者。解释的顺序反了过来：不是先有一个我再被投放进去，而是世界内部的过程产生这个我。')],pull:b('Not a self choosing a world, but a world giving rise to a self.','不是先有一个我，再选择世界；而是世界内部产生了这个我。')}
  ]},
  {id:'local-self',scene:4,title:b('I am not<br>the passenger.','我未必是乘客，<br>也可能是过程。'),deck:b('The observer belongs to the history being observed.','观察者属于他所观察的那段历史。'),symbol:'World → local process → “I”',caption:b('One local process is highlighted inside a larger history.','在更大的历史之中，一段局部过程被照亮。'),kind:inference,notes:[
    {n:8,type:inference,title:b('The self as a whirlpool','主体像水流形成的漩涡'),p:[
      b('If the self arises inside a world, “Why have I not jumped to another world?” may already contain the wrong assumption. There need not be a soul floating between A, B, and C. A generates its observer; B generates its observer. Each can call itself “I.”','如果主体在世界内部产生，“为什么我没有跳到另一个世界”可能已经包含错误前提。未必存在一个在 A、B、C 之间漂浮的灵魂。A 产生 A 的观察者，B 产生 B 的观察者，它们都可以称自己为“我”。'),
      b('A whirlpool is not an object that exists first and is then filled with water. A particular organization of water is the whirlpool. Likewise, rules, a body, continuous memory, a self-model, and a causal process may constitute a local subject. This is a proposed account of the subject’s organization; it still leaves the existence of subjective feeling to be explained.','漩涡不是先存在，再把水灌进去；特定的水流关系本身形成漩涡。同样，规则、身体、记忆连续、自我模型与因果过程，可能共同构成局部主体。这是在描述主体如何组织起来，仍未解释为什么会产生主观感受。')]},
    {n:9,type:inference,title:b('A complete history, an unknown future','完整历史与未知未来'),p:[
      b('Suppose A and B are identical until today, but tomorrow B contains an extraordinary event. The present observer cannot identify which complete history they belong to using the shared prefix alone. By contrast, a past event preserved in memory or other evidence can exclude histories inconsistent with that evidence.','假设 A、B 到今天为止完全一样，明天 B 却出现超常事件。当前观察者不能仅凭共享前缀，判断自己属于哪条完整历史。相反，过去事件若被记忆或证据保存，就能排除与这些证据不相容的历史。'),
      b('This is the asymmetry I was trying to express: the present carries records of some of the past, while it does not provide the whole future. Global completeness, if assumed, is not local omniscience. A history can be definite from a whole-world perspective while the future remains unknown from within it.','我想表达的不对称是：当前状态保存着部分过去，却不提供完整未来。即使假设全局结构完整，也不意味着局部观察者无所不知。从整体看确定的历史，对内部第一人称仍然可以是未知的。')]},
    {n:10,type:distinction,title:b('Determined does not mean causally irrelevant','确定，不等于没有因果意义'),p:[
      b('In a complete-history model, deliberation, effort, hesitation, and decisions all belong to the structure. Calling the history “fixed” does not remove their causal roles. A recorded football match has a definite score; the shot can still be the reason a goal occurs. The result being recorded does not erase the relationship between action and outcome.','在完整历史模型中，犹豫、努力、判断与决定都属于结构。把历史称为“确定”，并不会取消这些过程的因果作用。已经录完的足球比赛比分确定，但射门仍然可以是进球的原因。录像完成，不会抹去行动与结果之间的关系。'),
      b('I therefore separated two claims: an event is part of a complete history, and an event makes no difference causally. They are not the same. My effort can be both contained in the history and a cause of what follows. Global structure and internal causation answer different questions.','因此必须区分两件事：事件属于完整历史；事件在因果上无关紧要。二者并不相同。努力可以既是历史的一部分，又是后续事件的原因。全局结构与内部因果，回答的是不同问题。')],formula:b('Predetermined ≠ causally irrelevant\nGlobally complete ≠ locally known','历史确定 ≠ 因果无关\n全局完整 ≠ 局部已知')}
  ]},
  {id:'freedom',scene:5,title:b('Freedom is<br>not one variable.','自由，<br>不是一个变量。'),deck:b('The second revision separates what I can do from what makes a choice mine.','第二次修正：区分我能做什么，与什么让选择属于我。'),symbol:'Capacity / choice / awareness',caption:b('Different axes of freedom. No axis measures a person’s worth or establishes ultimate choice.','自由的不同维度；它们不衡量人的价值，也不证明终极选择权。'),kind:distinction,notes:[
    {n:11,type:revision,title:b('Capacity is not free will','能力自由不等于自由意志'),p:[
      b('I had been treating freedom as the amount of reality a subject can change. A human cannot fly unaided, teleport, or rewrite constants. An imagined being with extraordinary powers would have a larger set of reachable states. Yet even a million abilities do not establish that the final choice between them is independent of prior conditions.','此前我把自由理解为主体能改变多少现实。普通人不能任意飞行、瞬移或改写常数，设想中的超常存在拥有更大的可达集合。但即使拥有一百万种能力，也不能说明最终选哪一种，不受前因决定。'),
      b('The earlier intuition that “more variance means more freedom” conflated distinct questions. A broader counterfactual range concerns capacity. Ultimate authorship concerns choice. A wider action space is meaningful, but it does not settle the metaphysics of free will. I kept the first idea and renamed it control capacity, agency, or reachable range.','“variance 越大越自由”的直觉，混合了不同问题。更大的反事实范围涉及能力；最终选择源涉及选择权。更宽的行动空间有意义，却不能解决自由意志的形而上问题。我保留前者，并把它称为现实控制能力、agency 或可达范围。')]},
    {n:12,type:open,title:b('Between prior causes and randomness','在前因与随机之间'),p:[
      b('If a complete world already includes every act of thinking and choosing, a strong version of free will becomes difficult to preserve: with exactly the same past, state of the world, and self, could a genuinely different choice occur? A fixed complete history does not by itself provide that alternative.','若完整世界已经包含一切思考与选择，强自由意志就很难保留：在完全相同的过去、世界状态和自我之下，是否真正可以作出另一个选择？固定的完整历史本身并不提供这种另一种可能。'),
      b('A compatibilist reading remains available within this discussion: an action is mine because it arises through my desires, memory, judgment, values, and reasoning rather than external compulsion. “The world gives rise to me” and “I decide an action” need not conflict when I am part of the world. But this is distinct from being an irreducible ultimate source.','在这套讨论中，仍可以采用相容论式理解：行动之所以是我的，是因为它来自欲望、记忆、判断、价值与推理，而非外部强迫。“世界产生我”与“我决定行动”未必冲突，因为我本就是世界的一部分。但这与不可还原的终极选择源不同。'),
      b('The stronger problem remains open. If a choice follows entirely from prior causes, it can seem insufficiently free. If it has no cause at all, it begins to resemble randomness. What would “determined by me, yet neither predetermined nor random” actually mean? I do not yet have an answer.','更强的问题仍然开放：若选择完全由前因决定，似乎不够自由；若完全没有原因，又像随机。“由我决定，但既非被前因决定，也非随机”，究竟是什么意思？目前我没有答案。')]},
    {n:13,type:hypothesis,title:b('Permission levels, not a ranking of power','规则权限，不是战斗力排行'),p:[
      b('What I had called a “higher dimension” became more like a rule-access level, not necessarily a spatial dimension. An ordinary subject acts within allowed states; an imagined higher-access subject might invoke, modify, or create lower-level rules. If it remains constrained by meta-rules, the original question about an ultimate ground returns.','此前所谓“高维”，逐渐变成规则访问层级，而不一定是空间维度。普通主体在允许状态内行动；设想中的更高权限主体可能调用、修改或创造低层规则。如果它仍受 meta-rule 限制，关于终极层的问题就会再次出现。'),
      b('This is why immortals, gods, and Buddhist ideas should not be flattened into an RPG power ranking. Some imagined beings represent greater agency. Certain Buddhist questions, as I am using them here, point toward another axis: attachment to a fixed self and the division between subject and object. These are candidate comparisons, not claims that all traditions share one doctrine.','因此，仙、神与佛教观念不该被压成 RPG 战斗力排行。某些超常存在代表更大 agency；我在这里借用的某些佛教问题，则指向另一条轴：固定自我、我执与主客分离。这是候选比较方式，不是在断言不同传统共享同一教义。')],formula:b('What can I change?\nWhat determines my choice?\nHow well do I understand my constraints?','我能改变多少？\n什么决定了我的选择？\n我能理解多少自身限制？')}
  ]},
  {id:'first-person',scene:6,title:b('Why am I<br>here?','为什么，<br>是“我在这里”？'),deck:b('Explaining the organization of a self still leaves the felt center of experience.','解释主体的结构之后，体验的第一人称中心仍然存在。'),symbol:'Information → experience?',caption:b('The center marks a viewpoint. It does not explain why a viewpoint feels like anything.','中心标记了视角，却还没有解释视角为何带有感受。'),kind:open,notes:[
    {n:14,type:inference,title:b('Questioning the hidden allocation story','拆掉语言里的“分配模型”'),p:[
      b('After accepting that I belong to a world, the question returned: why this world? Language easily suggests a pre-existing true self standing beside a collection of worlds, waiting to be assigned. But the proposed model contains no allocation step. World A produces A’s subject; B produces B’s. A particular whirlpool belongs to its river because those local relations constitute it.','接受“我属于世界”以后，问题又变成：为什么偏偏是这个世界？语言很容易制造一个先于世界的真我，站在无数世界旁等待分配。但模型并没有分配这一步。A 产生 A 的主体，B 产生 B 的主体。具体漩涡属于这条河，因为这些局部关系构成了它。'),
      b('Removing that picture clarifies one question but does not dissolve the whole unease. There remains the first-person location of experience: why does any formed subject seem to occupy an absolute “here” from within? The organizational account does not automatically resolve that.','拆掉这个画面，澄清了一个问题，却没有消除全部困惑。仍然存在第一人称定位问题：为什么一个主体形成以后，从内部就会有一个绝对的“这里”？结构解释不会自动解决它。')]},
    {n:15,type:open,title:b('A self-concept is not the whole first person','自我概念，不等于第一人称本身'),p:[
      b('A self-concept includes a name, bodily ownership, memories, personality, and a social identity. Someone might lose much of that knowledge and still experience looking into a room or feeling pain. The deeper question is not only “How do I know who I am?” but “Why is there an experienced here at all?”','自我概念包含名字、身体归属、记忆、人格与社会身份。即使失去很多关于自己的知识，也仍可能体验到“我正在看这个房间”或“我在痛”。更深的问题不只是“我如何知道自己是谁”，而是“为什么会有一个被体验的这里”。'),
      b('Information processing, stable memory, and a self-model may describe how a system behaves as a self. They have not, within this framework, explained why anything feels like something from the inside. A being with more control over rules would still face this question if it had experience. Greater power need not erase first-person subjectivity.','信息处理、稳定记忆与自我模型，可以描述系统怎样表现得像一个自我；但在这个框架里，它们尚未解释为什么内部真的会有感觉。即使更高权限存在具有意识，它也仍可能面对这个问题。更大能力，未必取消第一人称性。'),
      b('One candidate idea is that different local subjects might be localizations of a more basic subjectivity. Expressions such as unity or a shared origin could be compared with that possibility. It would not mean that distinct personalities are empirically the same person. For now this is a candidate interpretation, not a conclusion.','一种候选想法是：不同局部主体，也许是更底层 subjectivity 的局部化。“一体”“同源”等表达可以与此比较，但这不意味着不同人格在经验层面就是同一个人。目前它只是候选解释，并非结论。')],pull:b('Why is there more than the processing of pain—why is there “I hurt”?','为什么不只是处理疼痛信息，而是“我疼”？')}
  ]},
  {id:'reflexivity',scene:7,title:b('The world builds<br>a model of itself.','世界的一部分，<br>为世界建立模型。'),deck:b('The inquiry loops back toward the conditions that made inquiry possible.','追问开始回到让追问得以发生的条件。'),symbol:'W → I → model(W) ⊂ W',caption:b('The model remains inside the world it tries to describe.','模型仍然属于它试图描述的世界。'),kind:inference,notes:[
    {n:16,type:inference,title:b('From observation to reflexivity','从观察，走向反身性'),p:[
      b('At first: I observe the world. Then: I am part of the world. Finally: a part of the world tries to understand the world that produced it. The world gives rise to consciousness; consciousness constructs a model of the world; that model remains an event within the world.','最初是“我在观察世界”；后来是“我是世界的一部分”；再后来，是“世界的一部分试图理解产生自己的世界”。世界产生意识，意识构造世界的模型，而模型本身仍然属于世界。'),
      b('Our senses, logic, language, and imagination may all be tools generated within a rule-governed world. Even realizing that our level might not be ultimate does not guarantee that we have concepts adequate to describe beyond it. But consciousness can also make its own conditions an object of thought: my body limits experience; my concepts shape my questions; I am using internal tools to speculate about an outside.','感官、逻辑、语言与想象力，可能都是规则世界内部产生的工具。意识到本层未必终极，并不保证拥有描述外部的概念。但意识又能把认知条件本身变成对象：身体限制体验，概念塑造问题，而我正使用内部工具推测外部。'),
      b('This suggested another dimension of freedom: meta-awareness, or understanding the structures that constrain me. Great external power need not bring reflective freedom. Limited power can coexist with recognition that bodily states, desires, personality, and the self-model are not absolute. That does not dissolve those constraints, but it changes how they are understood.','这提示了自由的另一维度：meta-awareness，即理解限制自己的结构。外部力量强大，未必带来认知自由；能力有限，也可能意识到身体、欲望、人格和自我模型并非绝对。这不会自动消除限制，但会改变对限制的理解。')]},
    {n:17,type:hypothesis,title:b('The provisional architecture','目前的临时框架'),p:[
      b('The framework begins with an imagined unrestricted ground, then complete possible worlds, then each world’s internal rules and structure. Some structures contain bodily continuity, memory, causal organization, and a self-model. Within such a history, an observer has a local perspective: traces of the past, no direct access to the complete future. Every step here keeps the epistemic status of its premises.','框架先设想不受最终外在禁止的可能性，再考虑完整可能世界，以及各世界内部的规则与结构。某些结构具有身体连续、记忆、因果组织和自我模型。历史内部的观察者拥有局部视角：保存过去痕迹，却不能直接读取完整未来。每一步都必须保留其前提的认识地位。'),
      b('Freedom then separates into control capacity, ultimate choice, awareness of constraints, and the extent of attachment to a fixed identity. Rule-access levels describe another possible hierarchy. The unresolved first-person problem cuts across these levels. Reflexivity connects them: a local observer can turn its explanatory tools back upon itself. This is a map of the questions, not a demonstrated cosmology.','自由进一步拆成控制能力、最终选择、对限制的认识，以及被固定身份束缚的程度。规则权限描述另一种候选层级；第一人称问题贯穿这些层级。反身性则把它们接起来：局部观察者能够反过来审查自己的解释工具。这是问题的地图，并非已证明的宇宙论。')],formula:b('Possibility → worlds → rules → local subjects\nLocal subjects → models → scrutiny of their own limits','可能性 → 世界 → 规则 → 局部主体\n局部主体 → 模型 → 审查自身的限制')}
  ]},
  {id:'open-questions',scene:8,title:b('Keep the<br>edges open.','让边界，<br>保持开放。'),deck:b('The discipline is to know which kind of claim I am making—and what it has not explained.','清楚自己正在提出哪一种主张，也清楚它尚未解释什么。'),symbol:'Experience / inference / hypothesis',caption:b('An unfinished boundary: the framework remains open to revision.','没有闭合的边界：框架仍然允许被修正。'),kind:open,notes:[
    {n:18,type:distinction,title:b('Three levels of commitment','区分经验、推论与形而上假设'),p:[
      b('<strong>Experience.</strong> Bodily state changes attention and the experienced world. Wishing does not arbitrarily rewrite external reality. Memory and bodily continuity participate in the everyday self. The observer does not directly read the future. These are the experiential starting points of the record.','<strong>经验层。</strong>身体状态改变注意力与可体验世界；意念不能任意改写外部现实；记忆与身体连续性参与日常自我；局部观察者不能直接读取未来。这些是记录的经验起点。'),
      b('<strong>Inference.</strong> Within the stated model, completeness of a history does not erase internal causation. A larger action space does not establish strong free will. Infinitely many possibilities do not imply equal probabilities. These distinctions do not by themselves prove the metaphysical premises around them.','<strong>推论层。</strong>在所述模型里，完整历史不取消内部因果；更大的行动空间不证明强自由意志；无限可能不意味着等概率。这些区分本身，并不证明围绕它们的形而上前提。'),
      b('<strong>Metaphysical hypothesis.</strong> No constrained layer is ultimate; an unrestricted ground exists; complete worlds actually coexist; higher levels can enter lower ones; subjects localize a shared subjectivity. Internal coherence alone does not establish any of these as facts. A theory that can absorb every observation risks losing the ability to distinguish anything.','<strong>形而上假设层。</strong>受限层都不是终极、存在无限可能的根基、完整世界实际并存、高层可进入低层、主体是共享主观性的局部化——内部自洽并不能把这些变成事实。能够吸收所有观察的理论，也可能失去区分任何情况的能力。')]},
    {n:19,type:open,title:b('Six questions the framework has not solved','六个仍未解决的问题'),p:[
      b('First, why is there definite structure at all? “The possible includes a rule-governed world” describes permission, not manifestation. Second, if all complete worlds exist, what does “exist” mean? Pursuing that question begins to challenge the concepts of world, logic, and possibility themselves.','第一，为什么存在确定结构？“可能性包含规则世界”解释了允许，却没有解释显现。第二，如果所有完整世界存在，“存在”是什么意思？继续追问，会开始挑战世界、逻辑、可能性这些概念本身。'),
      b('Third, why do some structures produce subjective feeling? Fourth, why does feeling have a first-person center? An account of information processing has not yet bridged either gap in this framework. They are related questions, but “a system models itself” is not a complete answer to “I am here.”','第三，为什么某些结构会产生主观感受？第四，感受为什么具有第一人称中心？在这个框架中，信息处理的描述尚未跨过这两道缺口。它们相关，但“系统建立自我模型”仍不是“我在这里”的完整答案。'),
      b('Fifth, can a subject be an irreducible source of choice, neither fully determined by prior causes nor merely random? Sixth, what evidence could distinguish cross-level information from dreams, error, coincidence, or unknown internal mechanisms? Any attempt to connect the speculation to experience must face that last question.','第五，主体能否成为不可还原的选择源，既不完全由前因决定，也非纯粹随机？第六，什么证据能把跨层信息，与梦、误判、巧合或未知内部机制区分开？形而上设想若要接触现实，必须面对最后这个检验问题。')]},
    {n:20,type:open,title:b('What the inquiry is really about','这条思路真正的中心'),p:[
      b('“Is the world virtual?” now seems too narrow. The thread runs through the limits of consciousness, the stability of rules, the emergence of a local subject, the continuity of its history, and the strange fact that it can question the conditions of its own existence. A real world need not, in this proposal, be ultimate reality. A local subject need not be a soul that predates it.','“世界是不是虚拟的”如今显得太窄。贯穿其中的是意识的权限、规则的稳定、局部主体的形成、历史的连续，以及主体竟能追问自身存在条件这一事实。在这个设想里，真实世界未必是终极实在，局部主体也未必是先于世界的灵魂。'),
      b('What I most want to retain is the way the thought evolved: begin with first-person experience; propose a structure; allow a contradiction to change it; separate experience, inference, and metaphysical hypothesis; treat myth and religion as possible comparisons rather than predetermined answers; then examine the tools of inquiry themselves.','我最想保留的是思考的演化方法：从第一人称经验出发，提出结构；让矛盾迫使模型改变；区分经验、推论与形而上假设；把神话与宗教作为候选比较材料，而非预设答案；最终反过来审查认知工具本身。'),
      b('The framework is unfinished. If we are local observers within a rule-governed world, remaining revisable may be one of the most faithful ways to take that condition seriously. The center of the inquiry is still this: a part of the world experiences “I am here,” and begins to ask why the whole of existence is as it is.','框架仍未完成。如果我们确实是规则世界内部的局部观察者，那么保持可修正性，也许正是认真对待这种处境的一种方式。追问的中心依然是：世界的一部分体验到“我在这里”，并开始追问整个存在为什么如此。')],pull:b('A part of the world begins to question the world that made it.','世界的一部分，开始追问产生自己的世界。')}
  ]}
];
